      "path": "plugin/cordis.patch.yml",
      "text": "# The @angela_lwh/dsh-archive-purge bundle patch: one row, applied over whatever layers came\n# before it. Installing this package as a profile bundle inserts the Host half;\n# the browser half needs no row of its own — `dsh-client-modules` finds it through\n# this package's `dsh.client` declaration and `exports[\"./client\"]`.\n#\n# A patch replaces the targeted row's whole `config`, so a profile overriding this\n# row must restate every key it means to keep. `sessionsRoot` is intentionally\n# absent: the Host half reads the live `session-persistence-jsonl` row's own root,\n# which is the only value that stays correct when a deployment relocates storage.\n\n- insert:\n    - id: archive-purge\n      name: \"@angela_lwh/dsh-archive-purge\"\n"
    }
